import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import Note from '../components/Note.astro';
---

<Doc
  title="About, license, contributing"
  kicker="Reference"
  description="Who maintains the OTAKU Manifesto, why it lives apart from PHPRise, and how the text is licensed."
  path="/about"
>
  <p class="lede">
    The philosophy outgrew the project that produced it. This site is where it lives
    now — independent of any language, package manager or vendor.
  </p>

  <h2>Why a separate home</h2>

  <p>
    OTAKU was written inside <a href="https://phprise.org">PHPRise</a>, a PHP
    foundation. That origin was an accident of the first implementation, not a property
    of the idea: the rules talk about indentation, collections, dependency direction and
    contracts, and every object-oriented language can express them.
  </p>

  <p>
    Keeping the manifesto inside a PHP organization made two mistakes at once. It
    implied the philosophy required PHP, and it made the PHP repositories carry a copy
    of a document that was not about them. PHPRise now links here instead of duplicating
    it.
  </p>

  <h2>Author</h2>

  <p>
    Written and maintained by
    <a href="https://esdras.me">Esdras Schönevald</a>, Lead Software Engineer and
    maintainer of PHPRise. The philosophy comes from two decades of building payment,
    identity and healthcare systems — and from the recurring experience that the
    expensive part of software is never the code you write, but the structure you keep.
  </p>

  <p>
    The intellectual debts are listed on the <a href="https://esdras.me/#inspirations">personal
    site</a>: Object Calisthenics (Jeff Bay), Clean Architecture (Robert C. Martin),
    DDD (Eric Evans), the Unix philosophy, Conway, Parnas and Dijkstra.
  </p>

  <h2>License</h2>

